# {{projectName}}

Custom Foldkit CN registry project generated from `foldkit-basic-cn-ui`.

## Project Layout

- `package.json` wires docs, registry generation, registry validation, tests, and typecheck scripts.
- `registry/config.json` owns the registry name, docs homepage, and registry base URL.
- `registry/default/items.json` is the source registry item manifest.
- `registry/templates/components.json` is the source `components.json` template.
- `registry/default/ui/example-card/` contains one example component slice.
- `registry/default/examples/example-card-basic/` contains one installable example.
- `apps/docs/public/components.json` and `apps/docs/public/r/*.json` are generated public registry output.
- `scripts/build-registry.mjs` builds the public registry JSON.
- `scripts/check-registry.mjs` validates the generated output.
- `scripts/serve-registry.ts`, `Dockerfile`, and `compose.yaml` serve the same generated registry locally or in a container.
- `src/` contains the docs app shell.

## Local Development

```bash
bun install
bun run dev
```

After editing files under `registry/default`, regenerate and check the registry:

```bash
bun run build:registry
bun run check:registry
bun run typecheck
bun run build
```

## Self-Hosted Registry

The generated registry server exposes:

- `/components.json` for shadcn registry alias configuration.
- `/r/{name}.json` for each generated registry item.
- Any additional generated public assets under `apps/docs/public/`.

The registry base URL is owned by `registry/config.json` and written into
`apps/docs/public/components.json` by `bun run build:registry`. For local
self-hosting, set it to a reachable URL such as `http://127.0.0.1:4174/r`, then
rebuild the registry.

```bash
bun run build:registry
bun run serve:registry -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4174
```

Smoke-test the registry from another terminal:

```bash
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:4174/components.json
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:4174/r/example-card.json
```

Container self-hosting builds the same generated artifacts into the image:

```bash
docker build -t {{projectName}}-registry .
docker run --rm -p 4174:4174 {{projectName}}-registry
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:4174/components.json
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:4174/r/example-card.json
```

Compose uses the same port mapping:

```bash
docker compose up --build registry
```
